{"sha": "f880a7f1e571b5a77c0224758388d971c9b45d20d54158e54d902046cd153ba3", "body": ["{\\small 材料的一生。橙色循环表示回收利用：", "旧物体的材料代替新的原料。}", "\\end{omfigure}", "", "\\section{分拣与回收利用}", "", "\\begin{definition}[回收利用]\\label{def:g5:raw-materials-and-recycling:recycling}", "\\emph{回收利用}\\index{回收利用}是收集用过的物体，", "并对其材料进行处理，使其能够用来制造新的物体，", "而不是被丢弃。", "\\end{definition}", "", "\\begin{proposition}[为什么要回收]\\label{prop:g5:raw-materials-and-recycling:why}", "% ledger: al:energy-primary, al:energy-recycled (8.3 / 186 = about 1/22)", "回收利用可以节省原料，这些原料无需从", "地下挖掘，而且通常还能节约能量。用旧易拉罐制造铝，", "所需能量只约为用铝土矿制造铝所需能量的二十分之一。", "这也意味着填埋场中的废弃物减少。", "\\end{proposition}", "", "\\begin{method}[分拣废弃物以便回收利用]\\label{met:g5:raw-materials-and-recycling:sort}", "回收利用从分拣开始，无论废弃物在哪里被丢弃：", "\\begin{enumerate}", "  \\item 玻璃瓶和广口瓶放入同一个垃圾桶；", "  \\item 金属罐、纸和纸板，以及塑料瓶，放入镇上为它们提供的", "        垃圾桶中（垃圾桶的颜色", "        因地而异）；", "  \\item 其余废弃物中无法回收利用的部分。", "\\end{enumerate}", "每种材料都有各自的回收方式，因此每个垃圾桶只能装", "它所对应的材料。", "\\end{method}", "", "\\begin{omfigure}", "\\begin{tikzpicture}[font=\\small]", "  \\foreach \\k/\\t/\\bc in {0/glass/green!50!black, 1/{metal cans}/gray,", "                        2/{paper and card}/omDef, 3/{plastic bottles}/orange!80!black} {", "    \\begin{scope}[xshift=\\k*3.4cm]", "      \\fill[\\bc!18, draw=\\bc, line width=0.8pt] (-1,0) -- (1,0) -- (1.15,2.0)", "        -- (-1.15,2.0) -- cycle;", "      \\fill[\\bc!45, draw=\\bc] (-1.25,2.0) rectangle (1.25,2.3);", "      \\node[anchor=north, align=center] at (0,-0.15) {\\t};", "    \\end{scope}", "  }", "  % glass: a bottle", "  \\fill[green!40!black!60] (-0.2,0.3) rectangle (0.2,1.2);", "  \\fill[green!40!black!60] (-0.07,1.2) rectangle (0.07,1.6);", "  % metal: a can", "  \\begin{scope}[xshift=3.4cm]", "    \\fill[black!25, draw=black!55] (-0.3,0.3) rectangle (0.3,1.3);", "  \\end{scope}", "  % paper: a box and a sheet", "  \\begin{scope}[xshift=6.8cm]", "    \\fill[brown!25, draw=brown!60] (-0.6,0.3) rectangle (0.1,1.0);", "    \\fill[white, draw=black!40] (0.2,0.3) rectangle (0.65,1.3);", "  \\end{scope}", "  % plastic: a bottle", "  \\begin{scope}[xshift=10.2cm]", "    \\fill[cyan!20, draw=cyan!50!black] (-0.25,0.3) rectangle (0.25,1.3);", "    \\fill[cyan!20, draw=cyan!50!black] (-0.1,1.3) rectangle (0.1,1.6);", "  \\end{scope}", "\\end{tikzpicture}", "", "{\\small 四个分类垃圾桶，每种材料一个。（真实垃圾桶的颜色", "各城镇之间有所不同。）}", "\\end{omfigure}", "", "\\begin{omfigure}", "\\begin{minipage}[t]{0.48\\linewidth}\\centering", "\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth,height=4.6cm,keepaspectratio]{images/book1/ai/g5-glass-cullet.jpg}", "", "{\\small 回收厂中待熔化的碎玻璃。}", "\\end{minipage}\\hfill", "\\begin{minipage}[t]{0.48\\linewidth}\\centering", "\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth,height=4.6cm,keepaspectratio]{images/book1/ai/g5-can-bales.jpg}", "", "{\\small 压扁后打包的铝制易拉罐。}", "\\end{minipage}", "\\end{omfigure}", "", "\\section{废弃物与资源}", "", "\\begin{definition}[资源]\\label{def:g5:raw-materials-and-recycling:resource}", "\\emph{资源}\\index{资源}是指一切取自自然界、人们所使用的东西：", "水、木材、矿石、石油、沙子。\\emph{可再生", "资源}\\index{可再生资源}是指在人的一生中能够自行再生或", "恢复的资源，例如经过补种的森林中的木材，或绵羊身上的羊毛。", "矿石和原油不可再生：一旦挖出", "并被使用，就不复存在了。", "\\end{definition}", "", "\\begin{proposition}[减少、再利用、回收利用]\\label{prop:g5:raw-materials-and-recycling:three}", "为使资源更持久，人们可以按以下顺序进行：", "\\begin{enumerate}", "  \\item \\textbf{减少}：少用物体，例如少用", "        包装物；", "  \\item \\textbf{再利用}：再次使用同一物体，例如把玻璃罐", "        重新装满，或把袋子带回商店；", "  \\item \\textbf{回收利用}：把材料制成新的物体。", "\\end{enumerate}", "回收利用排在最后，因为它仍需要能量和机器；", "最好的废弃物，是永远不被产生的那一种。", "\\end{proposition}", "", "\\section{练习}", "", "\\begin{exercise}[$\\star$]\\label{exo:g5:raw-materials-and-recycling:1}", "天然材料还是人造材料？木材、玻璃、羊毛、钢、塑料、石头。", "\\end{exercise}", ""]}